section.p:
SButtons are associated with a Scope Control constant in two ways:
in the constructor: SButton loginButton = new SButton(LoginController.VALIDATE_LOGIN);
via the SButton.setControlID(String controlString) method.

        To assign an image to SButton: 

        If you want to attach an icon to your button and you don't want the Control String to be displayed, call 
        SButton.setText("");  on the button after associating it with the Control.
        For example, 

SButton goSearch = new SButton(PatientSearchController.PROCESS_SEARCH); 
Icon searchIcon = (ImageLoader.loadImageIcon("SearchButton.jpg"))); 
goSearch.setIcon(searchIcon); 
goSearch.setText("");
